  "response": {
    "html": "<h1 data-chunk-id=\"d4eec69c-29b8-42d8-bcb3-7f766e339b27\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;border-bottom:3px solid #0d47a1;padding-bottom:6px\">Nebula Drift - Narrative</h1>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"643495ed-e31b-4a65-a214-fe5067492f82\" style=\"background-color:#e3f2fd;border-left:4px solid #1565c0;padding:8px 10px;font-size:9pt;color:#37474f\">Vantage Nine Studios - internal - sub-document of the Nebula Drift GDD.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"f457945b-0ead-42c5-9952-54f35e58ac89\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Premise</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"0a795d76-e89e-4b78-8219-2a2184e15d78\">The Drift Belt was a shipyard until it was not. Nobody agrees on what\nhappened and the only person still transmitting has a reason to lie.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"b5e62028-656b-4313-82e7-f7ef91513877\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Act I - Salvage</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"732b4a4b-8cf9-4e7e-96d0-1464deb616d0\">The player learns to move. Vex, on the channel, is helpful and slightly too\nwell informed about a place she claims never to have visited.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"1327a145-56ba-4676-a9c0-bcdd2009d685\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Act II - The Cartographer</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"c9767328-4b5e-49b9-b75e-0830004ff65c\">The wreck has been mapped before. The player starts finding the map, and it\nis annotated in Vex's hand.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"11591cb1-b8e6-42a8-9851-575471ac267d\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Act III - Drift</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"0cea856c-44c2-4eb8-baaf-4db48826c233\">The player can leave or finish the map. Both endings are short; neither is\nthe \"good\" one.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"7bab2fa0-a567-459a-8f8c-5578510044fe\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Characters</h2>\n<table data-chunk-id=\"ee73cd6f-690c-46de-baf6-dcb090bff8b5\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #37474f;font-family:Inter , Calibri , Arial , sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><thead><tr>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Character</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Role</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Voice</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">The Salvager</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Player</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Silent. Reads as competent, not heroic.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Vex</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Voice on the channel</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Warm, funny, unreliable.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">The Cartographer</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Antagonist, absent</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Never speaks. Only annotations.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>",
